Source: moos-ivp-helm
Section: libs
Priority: optional
Maintainer: Toby Schneider <toby@gobysoft.org>
Build-Depends: debhelper-compat (= 13),
               cmake
Standards-Version: 4.7.0
Rules-Requires-Root: no
Homepage: https://moos-ivp.org
Vcs-Git: https://github.com/GobySoft/moos-ivp.git -b ivp-without-moos
Vcs-Browser: https://github.com/GobySoft/moos-ivp/tree/ivp-without-moos

Package: libivp-helm0
Architecture: any
Multi-Arch: same
Depends: ${shlibs:Depends}, ${misc:Depends}
Description: IvP helm libraries built without MOOS
 MOOS-IvP includes software for high-level control (decision-making) on
 robotic platforms (primarily marine). IvP stands for "Interval
 Programming", a mathematical programming model for multi-objective
 optimization; the IvP Helm represents and reconciles the output of its
 behaviors with it.
 .
 This package provides lib_helmivp (the helm engine, behavior sets and
 behavior factory) and the libraries it links, built as shared libraries
 without MOOS, MOOSGeodesy or FLTK, for running the helm outside MOOS. They
 are installed under /usr/lib/<multiarch>/ivp-helm, so they can coexist with
 the libmoos-ivp packages.

Package: libivp-helm-dev
Section: libdevel
Architecture: any
Multi-Arch: same
Depends: libivp-helm0 (= ${binary:Version}), ${misc:Depends}
Description: IvP helm libraries built without MOOS (development files)
 MOOS-IvP includes software for high-level control (decision-making) on
 robotic platforms (primarily marine). IvP stands for "Interval
 Programming", a mathematical programming model for multi-objective
 optimization; the IvP Helm represents and reconciles the output of its
 behaviors with it.
 .
 This package provides the headers and CMake package of the helm libraries
 built without MOOS. Find them with
 find_package(IVP CONFIG) after adding /usr/lib/<multiarch>/ivp-helm to
 CMAKE_PREFIX_PATH, and link the IVP::helmivp, IVP::behaviors, ... targets.
